==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|svá|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*swa}}, {{m|gem-pro|*swē}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*swe}} and {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*se}}. Cognate with Old English {{m|ang|swā}} (English {{term|so|lang=en}}), Old Frisian {{term|sa|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{m|osx|sō}}, Dutch {{term|zo|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{m|goh|sō}} (German {{term|so|lang=de}}), Swedish {{term|så|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|så|lang=da}}, Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍅𐌰|lang=got}}, Latin {{term|si|lang=la}} (from an earlier form {{term|suad|lang=la}}), Oscan {{term|𐌔𐌅𐌀𐌝|sc=Ital|lang=osc|tr=svaí}}, Umbrian {{term|sve|lang=xum}}, Greek {{term|ὡς|lang=grc}} (earlier '''*ϝος''').

